# ============================================================
#  Expansion — one more event per elective, plus a core-class
#  event everyone can get.
# ============================================================

@event core_flying_lesson
slot: morning
title: Compulsory Broom Flight
class: routine
tone: tense
when: year == 1 and month <= 6 and term
weight: 12
art: broom
tags: class danger
scene: A row of nervous first-years standing beside brooms on the lawn, one broom already rising on its own, an instructor with a whistle.
text: Compulsory first-year broom flight. The instructor blows her whistle. Your broom rises, hesitates, and then — clearly having taken a dislike to you — begins drifting toward the lake.
> left: Hold on and steer it back
  challenge feat apprentice wild:
    win:
      vigor +small
      renown +small
      say: You wrestle it round and land, wobbling, exactly on the mark. The instructor nods. The broom grudgingly accepts you.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: The broom wins. You land in the shallows. Everyone sees. Everyone remembers.
> right: Jump off while it's still low
  mood -tiny
  vigor +tiny
  say: You drop four feet onto the grass. Undignified, but dry. The broom carries on to the lake alone and sinks with a sulky gurgle.

@event pyro_dragon_breath
title: A Sample of Dragonfire
class: routine
tone: light
track: evocation
weight: 12
art: dragon
tags: class magic
scene: A glass jar containing a single writhing flame of deep blue, held in tongs by a stern professor, students leaning back from it.
text: Thorne holds up a sealed jar containing one flame of genuine dragonfire, blue-white and furious. "Who would like to try holding it?" he asks. Nobody moves. He looks at you.
> left: Hold it
  challenge spell standard+1:
    win:
      arcana +medium
      renown +small
      rel thorne +small
      say: It sears and struggles and then, astonishingly, settles in your palm like a small warm animal. The class stares. Thorne almost smiles.
    lose:
      health -large
      say: The dragonfire disagrees. You spend a week with bandaged hands and a new respect for dragons.
> right: Watch someone else
  lore +tiny
  say: A fourth-year volunteers and loses a sleeve. You take careful notes on what not to do.

@event tide_water_spirit_race
title: The Water Spirit Race
class: routine
tone: light
track: evocation
weight: 12
art: wave
tags: class nature
scene: Students swimming across a lake at dawn, translucent water-spirits racing alongside them like silver dolphins.
text: Professor Marisol's final challenge: swim the lake while the water spirits race you. "They cheat," she says cheerfully. "Ask them nicely not to."
> left: Race them flat out
  challenge feat journeyman wild:
    win:
      vigor +medium
      renown +small
      say: You touch the far shore a hand's length ahead of the fastest spirit. It sulks, then laughs like a fountain.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: The spirits tow you in circles. You arrive last, but very clean.
> right: Ask them nicely
  challenge negotiate apprentice+:
    win:
      mood +medium
      arcana +tiny
      say: You ask. They carry you across on their backs like a raft. Marisol says that counts. Marisol says it's the whole point.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: They pretend not to hear. Water spirits are terrible at manners.

@event illusion_mirror_maze
title: The Mirror Maze Exam
class: routine
tone: light
track: illusion
weight: 12
art: mirror
tags: class magic
scene: A maze of tall mirrors in a dark hall, each reflecting a different version of the same student, one reflection grinning.
text: Professor Vey's exam: a maze of enchanted mirrors. Find the exit. Some reflections lie. One of them is — she promises — the real you.
> left: Trust your own eyes
  challenge deceive standard:
    win:
      guile +medium
      study illusion +tiny
      say: You spot the reflection that blinks late, and follow it out. Vey awards top marks and says, "Most people trust the one that looks happiest."
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: You follow the happiest reflection for an hour. It leads you in a circle and waves goodbye.
> right: Shatter the illusion
  challenge spell standard:
    win:
      arcana +small
      study illusion +tiny
      say: Every mirror goes dark at once. Exit found. Vey writes, "Effective. Inelegant. Pass."
    lose:
      health -small
      say: You shatter one mirror. It was real. Seven years of bad luck, the caretaker says, or three crowns for the glass.
      gold -tiny

@event alch_love_potion
title: The Love Potion Assignment
pool: alchemy_class_weight12
tone: warm
art: potion
tags: romance
scene: A pink, glittering potion in a heart-shaped flask on a workbench, a student holding it up to the light with a doubtful expression.
text: This week's assignment: brew a love potion — "for analytical purposes only". Your flask glows a suspicious pink. Someone at the next bench asks if they can buy it. Several people ask.
> left: Brew it perfectly, then pour it away
  alchemy +medium
  study alchemy +tiny
  say: Perfect colour, perfect scent. You pour it down the sink. The pipes are affectionate for a week.
> right: Sell it
  alignment -small
  gold +medium
  chance unlikely:
    gain detention
    say: A prefect falls in love with the headmistress's portrait. It's traced back to you. Worth it, almost.
  else:
    say: Fifteen crowns. You never ask what it was used for. You see a lot of unusual couples at dinner.

@event div_prophecy_exam
title: The Prophecy Exam
class: routine
tone: eerie
track: astromancy
weight: 12
art: eye
tags: class mystery
scene: A dim divination classroom, a single student staring into a crystal ball, the examiner's quill hovering expectantly over a blank page.
text: The mock Divination exam: gaze into the crystal and make one prophecy about the coming month. The examiner will check. "Vague prophecies," she warns, "fail."
> left: Make a bold, specific prophecy
  chance even:
    study astromancy +medium
    renown +small
    say: "On the eighth, the kitchen cat will have kittens in the headmistress's hat." On the eighth, she does. Top marks in the mock.
  else:
    study astromancy -small
    say: "On the eighth, it will snow indoors." It does not snow indoors. The examiner writes "ambitious".
> right: Make a careful, safe prophecy
  study astromancy +tiny
  lore +tiny
  say: "Someone will be late to breakfast." Someone is. The examiner sighs and gives you a bare pass: it was vague, but it was checkable.
> up[omen]: Foretell it, out loud, so it lands
  study astromancy +small
  mood -tiny
  say: You say it plainly, in that flat certain voice: the examiner's kettle will boil dry on Friday. It does. She gives you full marks and looks at you as if you'd done it on purpose. You aren't sure you didn't.

@event art_golem_helper
title: The Little Golem
class: routine
tone: light
track: artifice
weight: 12
art: gear
tags: class magic
scene: A knee-high clay golem carrying a teetering stack of books across a classroom, a student watching anxiously as it nears a staircase.
text: Your term project: a knee-high clay golem that carries books. It works! It works so well that it has started carrying everyone's books, whether they want it to or not.
> left: Add a "stop" command
  challenge research standard-2:
    win:
      study artifice +small
      lore +small
      say: The golem stops. It also waits politely. The professor asks if she can borrow it for her office.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: Now it stops randomly, mid-staircase, holding forty books. Nobody can get past it. It looks very pleased.
> right: Let it roam free
  chance likely:
    renown +small
    mood +small
    say: The golem becomes a beloved castle fixture, delivering books to whoever looks sad. It signs every delivery with your initials, in clay.
  else:
    renown -tiny
    say: It also delivers a Restricted Section book to a first-year. The librarian follows the clay smudges straight to your door.

@event beast_hippocampus
title: The Hippocampus Foal
pool: beastcraft_class_weight12
tone: light
art: wave
tags: nature
scene: A tiny sea-horse foal with a fish's tail struggling in a rock pool on the lake shore, a student kneeling beside the water.
text: A hippocampus foal — half pony, half fish — has been stranded in a shrinking rock pool on the lakeshore. Professor Brask is on the other side of the grounds. The foal is panicking.
> left: Carry it to the lake
  alignment +tiny
  challenge feat apprentice:
    win:
      mood +medium
      vigor +tiny
      say: It thrashes, then trusts you. You wade out and let it go. It circles you three times before diving deep.
    lose:
      health -small
      mood +small
      say: It kicks you in the stomach with surprising force — but you get it to the water. Brask says that's how they say thank you.
> right: Run for Professor Brask
  lore +small
  say: Brask arrives with a bucket and a lullaby. She makes you hold the bucket. You learn more in ten minutes than in a whole term.

@event astro_eclipse
when: not closed(hollowstar)
title: The Eclipse
class: story
tone: eerie
track: astromancy
weight: 12
art: moon
tags: class mystery
scene: A black disc sliding across the sun above the observatory dome, students on the roof with smoked-glass lenses, a halo of light around the darkness.
text: An eclipse, the first in forty years. The astromancy class is on the roof with smoked-glass lenses. At the moment of totality, you notice something the charts don't show: a second shadow, smaller, moving the wrong way.
> left: Record it precisely
  lore +medium
  find second_shadow
  say: You chart the second shadow's path exactly. It crosses the sky and stops — directly above the lake.
> right: Just watch the eclipse
  mood +medium
  say: For four minutes the world holds its breath. You'll remember the cold, and the silence, and the strange birdsong, for the rest of your life.

@event heal_triage_drill
title: Triage
pool: alchemy_class_weight12
tone: tense
art: cross
tags: danger
scene: A practice ward full of students acting injured, groaning theatrically on cots, a single student healer in the middle with a clipboard.
text: Sister Amaranth's triage drill: twelve "injured" students, one healer — you — and ten minutes. Some are faking worse than others. One, you realise, is genuinely hurt.
> left: Treat the genuine injury first
  challenge brew standard-1:
    win:
      alchemy +medium
      study alchemy +tiny
      say: You spot the real injury in the first minute. Amaranth nods, once, which is the highest honour in the infirmary.
    lose:
      study alchemy +tiny
      say: You find the real injury in minute nine. Late, but not too late. Amaranth's lips thin. "Again tomorrow."
> right: Work systematically down the line
  study alchemy +tiny
  lore +tiny
  say: Methodical, thorough and slow. The real patient waits seven minutes. Amaranth makes you write an essay on why.

@event umbral_last_lecture
title: The Last Lecture on Absence
class: story
tone: eerie
when: year >= 2
track: umbral
weight: 12
art: skull
tags: class mystery hollowstar
thread: hollowstar
scene: An Umbral Theory lecture hall lit only by a black candle, the professor drawing a star with a hollow centre on the board.
text: The Umbral professor draws a star with a hollow centre on the board. "This is not on the syllabus," she says. "Three hundred years ago this academy imprisoned an absence that thinks. I believe you should know that before you graduate."
> left: Take careful notes
  lore +medium
  flag knows_founders_seal
  find knows_founders_seal
  hs_omens_progress
  find seven_locks
  say: She speaks for an hour about seals and locks and the founders' fear. At the end she wipes the board clean and says, "This lecture never happened."
> right: Ask why she's telling you
  rel isolde +tiny
  say: "Because something is stirring," she says, "and the headmistress asked me to find out which of you would ask that question." She writes your name down.
